  {
    "pkattachmentId": 72343,
    "bookid": 65,
    "chapterId": 169,
    "fileId": 34801,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;9.02</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Cysts in the differential diagnosis of orbital dermoid cysts</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Hind Alkatan",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 769px; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.562px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cyst type</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lining</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Other characteristics</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.562px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival cyst</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{678180;9267597;9782472}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Non-keratinizing stratified squamous epithelium and goblet cells but without appendages</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Tumour tends to present later in life, is usually soft, results in minor symptoms (eyelid fullness with no proptosis), and is mostly anterior and superomedial in location without bony defect</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.562px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival dermoid cyst</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{678180}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Non-keratinizing stratified squamous epithelium with goblet cells and adnexal structures in the wall</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Symptoms usually develop over years; usually involves the superomedial quadrant of the orbit, lacks osseous defect, and may cause proptosis <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{12045960}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.562px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Epidermoid cyst</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{25276416}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Keratinizing stratified squamous epithelium with absent adnexal structures</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Can be either primary (congenital) or secondary (implantation);<sup>a</sup> the primary cysts are usually slowly growing and deep in the orbit, and present at a relatively older age</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.562px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Respiratory epithelial choristomatous cyst</span></strong><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{4088630;11766031;25314310;27097398}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pseudostratified ciliated columnar epithelium with goblet cells, filled with mucoid material; believed to arise from sequestered respiratory epithelium from paranasal sinuses during development</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Located in orbital sites that are atypical for dermoids but may be associated with bony defect <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{12213161}</span>; has been reported also in the eyelid <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{33063330}</span>; usually follow a benign course but may result in strabismus and amblyopia in young children <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{25314310}</span>; can be intraconal in location causing difficulty in the management <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{27097398}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.562px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Choristomatous lacrimal gland cyst</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{9267597;7270633}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Thin ductal epithelial lining with or without fibrous capsule and adjacent nest of ectopic lacrimal gland tissue</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Develops in relation to ectopic lacrimal gland tissue with ductal-like cyst formation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.562px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Ossifying cystic odontogenic and Schneiderian choristoma</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{24171664}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lined by Schneiderian cystic epithelium with adjacent mucinous oral glands, tooth, and lamellar bone</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">A single reported case of a 12-year-old girl with infraorbital-located recurrent mass <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{24171664}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.562px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Phakomatous choristoma</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{10406159;31640459}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Islands of lenticular-like material surrounded by thick basement membrane</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Rare, benign congenital tumour of lenticular anlage that can be partially cystic; almost always located in the medial lower eyelid and anterior orbit</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.562px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Others</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.15625px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"3%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 126.031px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cystic teratoma </span></strong><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{25530304}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Teratomatous cyst showing tissue from two to three germ cell layers</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Teratomas can be either mature or immature and their clinical diagnosis might be challenging <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{24413870;29755277}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.15625px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"3%\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 126.031px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Congenital cystic eye </span></strong><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{12841852;25530304}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">A thin-walled cyst with no identifiable ocular structures</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Rare; diagnosed at birth; may attain large size and be associated with facial dermal appendages</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.15625px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"3%\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 126.031px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Microphthalmos with cyst </span></strong><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{35347187}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cystic portion lined by retinal and neuroglial tissue</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cyst is found in relation to microphthalmic globes with coloboma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.15625px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"3%\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 126.031px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"18%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Haematic cyst </span></strong><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{29755271}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.141px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cyst with reactive fibrosis and pseudocapsule formation but no epithelial lining; haemorrhage and haemosiderin deposits are common with possible formation of cholesterol granuloma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 288.172px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Etiology is unclear but might be related to a pre-existing vascular lesion; mean age of 44&nbsp;years at presentation; diagnosis can be aided by radiological findings</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Secondary implantation cysts in the orbit may arise from conjunctival or respiratory epithelium after trauma, surgery, or chronic sinus disease <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{3964639;24359804}</span>, or from ectopic lacrimal gland tissue <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{10820914}</span><span class=\"ParaTextChar\">.</span></span></p>",
